xnu 0376: print the blank timer and its gate

Measured 2026-11-19: `mondrianfb_blank=30` was on the command line, the kernel's
own boot line showed it, and the driver still logged no idle blank, while the
same driver blanked on the power key and, with the default of 1 s, blanked by
itself. Print the parsed seconds at setup and, behind `mondrianbtrace=1`, the
age of the last present and the input grace once every ten seconds.

The line answered it on the first boot: the parsed seconds read 0, because
`PE_parse_boot_argn` keeps the last occurrence of a key and the board's
`mondrianfb_blank=0` came after the test value. With the test value last, the
same trace counted the gate to 30 and the driver logged `panel blank after 30
s without a frame`, `panel wake (touch)` and `panel on (dcs)`. It changes no
decision.

